stock) in exchange for their shares of the target, and the acquirer ends up=
 owning the target corporate entity.</li> <li style=3D"margin-bottom: 5px;"=
>The acquirer&nbsp;buys&nbsp;the&nbsp;<em>assets&nbsp;</em>of the company, =
in an asset purchase; the target company gets something (cash, acquirer sto=
ck) in exchange for its business. If the target is selling&nbsp;<em>all&nbs=
p;</em>of its assets, it will be left as an empty shell, and will probably =
distribute the cash or stock to its shareholders and liquidate.</li> </ol> =
